1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,410
You wake up in 1962,

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:06,130
locked inside a maximum security prison.

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:07,510
Alcatraz.

4
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,530
The one nobody escapes.

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,250
Here's how you get out.

6
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:11,940
Step one:

7
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,650
the wall.

8
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:13,940
It's concrete,

9
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:16,830
but decades of salt air have rotted it.

10
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,000
And behind the air vent in your cell

11
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,450
is an unguarded service corridor.

12
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,670
So you dig around the vent.

13
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,800
With a spoon from the mess hall.

14
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,690
But scraping is loud.

15
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:30,040
So you build a drill from a vacuum

16
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:30,940
cleaner motor,

17
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,450
and muffle it.

18
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,120
Then cover whatever's left by playing

19
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,590
accordion during daily music hour.

20
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,870
But now there's a hole in your wall.

21
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:42,260
So you make a fake vent cover from

22
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,630
painted cardboard.

23
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:44,880
In dim light,

24
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,610
the guards see a wall.

25
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,570
Now you can reach the corridor.

26
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:51,550
But you can't swim San Francisco Bay.

27
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,710
So you collect raincoats.

28
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:54,580
More than fifty.

29
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:56,860
You glue them into a raft,

30
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:59,140
and seal the seams with heat from the

31
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,150
steam pipes.

32
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,970
But when you slip out at night,

33
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,370
guards check your bed.

34
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:05,850
So you sculpt a head from plaster,

35
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:06,400
soap,

36
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,610
and toilet paper.

37
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,250
Real hair from the barber shop.

38
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:11,260
In the dark,

39
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,450
it looks asleep.

40
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,060
June 11th.

41
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,690
Four men plan to go.

42
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:16,980
But one of them,

43
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:17,700
Allen West,

44
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:18,430
is stuck.

45
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,860
The cement he used to hide his hole

46
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,890
has hardened.

47
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,340
The others can't wait.

48
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,470
They leave without him.

49
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:26,790
Up the pipes.

50
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,210
Onto the roof.

51
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,690
Over the fences.

52
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:32,320
Down to a shoreline the searchlights

53
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:33,430
can't see.

54
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,940
They inflate the raft and paddle out

55
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,800
into 54 degree water,

56
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,850
aiming for Angel Island.

57
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,500
At dawn,

58
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,660
the guards find three men sleeping.

59
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:44,510
Until they touch one.

60
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,270
A paddle turns up.

61
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,550
Scraps of a raincoat raft.

62
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:51,170
The FBI searches for years.

63
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,810
In 1979,

64
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:55,340
the FBI closed the case,

65
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,590
presuming them dead.

66
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:59,690
But no confirmed body was ever found.

67
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,290
Maybe they drowned.

68
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:03,030
Maybe they made it.
